---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About Belinda Dunne | Auckland Boudoir Photographer"
  description="Meet Belinda Dunne, an Auckland boudoir photographer with a master's in photography focused on posing and lighting, helping women see themselves in a new light."
>
  <!-- Hero: full-bleed photo with heading + CTA -->
  <section class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/about/hero.jpg"
      alt=""
      style="object-position: 45.082% 0%;"
      class="h-[420px] w-full object-cover sm:h-[480px]"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 px-6 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl text-boudoir-pink md:text-5xl">Meet your Auckland boudoir photographer</h1>
      <a
        href="/contact-boudoir-photography-auckland"
        class="inline-block border-2 border-boudoir-pink px-6 py-3 text-boudoir-pink hover:bg-boudoir-pink hover:text-boudoir-ink"
      >
        Contact me today
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro: portrait + bio -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
      <img
        src="/images/about/belinda-portrait.jpg"
        alt="Belinda Dunne, Auckland boudoir photographer, looking out the window"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        width="1600"
        height="1600"
      />

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl">I <strong>love taking clients from:</strong></h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">
          <strong><em>&ldquo; </em>I don't look good in photographs&rdquo;</strong>
          <br />
          <strong>to</strong>
          <br />
          <strong>&ldquo;OMG is that really me<em>&rdquo;</em></strong>
        </h3>

        <p class="mt-6 text-boudoir-muted">
          I've always been passionate about <strong>empowering women to feel
          beautiful and confident</strong> in their own skin. My journey started in
          the events industry, where I worked to improve the representation
          of <strong>female athletes in the media</strong>. But I wanted to do
          more&mdash;I wanted to help <strong>every-day women</strong> see
          themselves in a new light.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-boudoir-muted">
          That's why I turned my much loved-hobby into a career and became a{" "}
          <strong>boudoir photographer</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Full-bleed photo with the rest of her story -->
  <section class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/home/tiled-floor-face-down.jpg"
      alt=""
      class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
    />
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-24 text-center text-boudoir-white">
      <p>I hear all the time:</p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        &ldquo;I never look good in photos.&rdquo; But here's the truth: it's
        not you.
        <br />
        It's bad lighting, bad angles, and the bullshit we've been fed about
        beauty for years.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        I've spent years mastering how to light and pose every body type, at
        every size and every age, to bring out what makes you magnetic. Every curve, every expression,
        every little moment&mdash;we'll capture it all. This isn't just
        photography. It's transformation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        When you see your final images, you won't just see beauty.
        <br />
        You'll see strength, sensuality, softness, fire&mdash;everything that
        makes you you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
